+# Meeting authority PR B: derivative provenance and review-gated promotion
+
+**Issue:** `9558cfaa-e34d-4412-9b8c-a84c28873387`
+**Parent:** `bdd55b7e-2acb-43a4-847d-55a2acb11571`
+**Classification:** Critical - authorization, additive data migration, AI-assisted writes
+**Stage:** PLAN review; no DEV, push, or PR authority
+**Base:** `origin/main@42e30d88bc516dc6472c9f1bb837bd694844aa47`
+**Worktree:** `.worktrees/meeting-authority-pr-b-plan` on `codex/meeting-authority-pr-b-plan`
+
+## Outcome
+
+Deliver the second caller-authority train unit as a sequence of medium, reviewable
+stack layers. A generated summary remains a stable, meeting-owned, versioned
+artifact; an extracted action item becomes a separate meeting-owned review
+candidate. Both use the compact mixed-content card shell: type/icon, concise
+title, one source/reason line, and no more than three verified chips or links.
+
+No extractor, finalizer, provider, model, background job, refresh, or adjustment
+creates a Product-Suite task/work item. Summary cards expose `Adjust` and
+`Dismiss`, never `Add`; revision changes only the meeting-owned summary artifact.
+Action-candidate cards expose `Add`, `Adjust`, and `Dismiss`. Action `Add` is the
+only promotion command: it applies the displayed immutable candidate version,
+preserves the meeting conversation as the access origin, and converges to exactly
+one restricted work item. Action `Adjust` offers at most these three natural-
+language planning choices:
+
+1. `Make this a simple task`
+2. `Turn this into a planned work item`
+3. `Keep this as a meeting follow-up`
+
+`Dismiss` removes the subject from the review queue without deleting its source
+evidence and creates no Product-Suite record. Summary and action adjustments use
+the existing collaboration event and agent-run protocol and append only immutable
+subject-specific versions. Unknown, ambiguous, stale, cross-tenant, unauthorized, or weakly
+supported owner/date/parent/dependency values are absent from the canonical
+version and remain unset on Add.
+
