+## Success criteria
+
+1. Summary sources materialize versioned meeting artifacts, and action-item
+   sources materialize action candidates, without creating proposals, memories,
+   tasks, work items, or dependencies.
+2. Meeting source, access conversation, summary artifact/version, action
+   candidate/version, actor, agent run, collaboration events, proposal, work item,
+   and suggestion evidence are
+   linked through same-tenant constraints and explicit internal projections.
+3. Every existing meeting and meeting-derived direct read, list, action,
+   retrieval, ranking, proposal, work-item child, and tool path evaluates the
+   authenticated caller's current membership before content leaves its
+   repository. Missing origin denies.
+4. Search/list/injection paths omit denied rows before counts, ranking, model
+   input, or projection. Direct IDs return the same not-found result for missing
+   and denied resources.
+5. Only an action candidate accepts `Add`; it is authenticated, writer-authorized,
+   stale-version fenced, idempotent, and exactly-once at the work-item boundary.
+   Summary Add is absent from codecs, routes, UI, and database transitions.
+6. At most three suggestions are attached to a version. Each is high-confidence,
+   evidence-referenced, same-tenant, currently caller-visible, and exactly typed.
+   Add applies only suggestion IDs visibly presented and confirmed by the click.
+7. `Adjust` appends a caller event and agent event to the existing meeting
+   conversation, mints one attributable `agent_runs` row, validates bounded
+   structured output, and appends one immutable version. It has no write tools.
+8. Summary-artifact and action-candidate state machines are independently
+   enforced. Dismiss is durable across refresh/retry and cannot be reopened by
+   source rematerialization or a late adjustment response.
+9. API responses use named, versioned projections. Internal origin, evidence,
+   confidence, request hashes, denial reasons, prompts, and raw source content do
+   not escape card/result responses.
+10. The platform-web experience covers loading, empty, error, stale, in-flight,
+    revised, added, dismissed, and unauthorized states with WCAG 2.2 AA keyboard,
+    focus, announcement, contrast, zoom, and responsive behavior.
+11. Unit, route, contract, migration, real-Neon, and Playwright suites prove the
+    Alice/Bob/Carol/Dave matrix, revocation, concurrency, retry, compatibility,
+    response keys, and zero automatic work creation.
+
