+## Selected architecture
+
+### One access origin and one promotion boundary
+
+`meetings.conversation_id` from PR A remains the sole access origin. Summary
+artifact/version, action candidate/version, suggestion, command, proposal, legacy
+meeting derivative, work item, and work-item child access follows that origin.
+Current active conversation membership is checked on every request/read; positive
+decisions are request-local.
+
+Source materialization writes only meeting-owned review state. Summary adjustment
+appends a summary-artifact version and never enters the promotion boundary.
+Action `Add` creates or reuses one conversation-scoped proposal and immediately
+applies it through the existing validated work-item domain command as the
+authenticated human's explicit approval. It is not a second Inbox click. The
+applied proposal remains the audit record and exactly-once anchor.
+
+Action-candidate destination is versioned as `simple_task` or
+`planned_work_item`; both create one restricted work item. `meeting_follow_up` is
+an Adjust planning choice, not a destination enum: accepting that choice dismisses
+the action candidate from promotion while preserving its revised text as meeting
+evidence in the conversation. Decision and follow-up evidence remains in the
+meeting domain in MVP and is never silently duplicated into memory.
+
+### Exact database schema
+
+The migration uses the canonical Neon root and next revision supplied by merged
+PR A. Names below are final; only the numeric revision placeholder changes.
+
