+#### `meeting_action_candidate_suggestions`
+
+Only verified, high-confidence, same-tenant suggestions are persisted. Absence is
+the representation of uncertainty; there is no unresolved/null suggestion row.
+
+| Column | Definition |
+|---|---|
+| `id` | UUID PK, generated |
+| `tenant_id` | TEXT NOT NULL |
+| `version_id` | UUID NOT NULL |
+| `kind` | `meeting_candidate_suggestion_kind` NOT NULL |
+| `position` | SMALLINT NOT NULL, `0..2` |
+| `confidence` | REAL NOT NULL, `0.80..1.0` |
+| `owner_actor_id` | UUID NULL; owner only |
+| `due_date` | DATE NULL; due-date only |
+| `work_item_id` | UUID NULL; parent/dependency only |
+| `evidence_refs` | JSONB NOT NULL; 1-8 opaque source IDs/windows, never quotes |
+
+Checks require exactly the typed value for `kind`; unique `(version_id,position)`
+and `(version_id,kind,coalesced-value)` prevent duplicates. Position bounds make
+more than three chips structurally impossible. Add receives and revalidates the
+displayed suggestion IDs; no unconfirmed or hidden row is applied.
+
+#### Separate command ledgers
+
+`meeting_summary_commands` uses `(tenant_id,summary_artifact_id,expected_version_id,
+kind,idempotency_key,request_hash,status,actor_id,run_id,user_event_id,
+agent_event_id,result_version_id,error_code,timestamps)`. Its kind enum contains
+only `adjust|dismiss`, making summary Add structurally impossible.
+
+`meeting_action_candidate_commands` uses:
+
+| Column | Definition |
+|---|---|
+| `id` | UUID PK, generated |
+| `tenant_id` | TEXT NOT NULL |
+| `candidate_id` | UUID NOT NULL |
+| `expected_version_id` | UUID NOT NULL |
+| `kind` | `meeting_action_command_kind` NOT NULL |
+| `idempotency_key` | TEXT NOT NULL, 1-200 chars |
+| `request_hash` | TEXT NOT NULL; canonical semantic request hash |
+| `status` | `meeting_review_command_status` NOT NULL |
+| `actor_id` | UUID NOT NULL; server-derived caller actor |
+| `run_id` | UUID NULL; Adjust only |
+| `user_event_id`,`agent_event_id` | UUID NULL; Adjust only |
+| `result_version_id` | UUID NULL; Adjust only |
+| `proposal_id` | UUID NULL; Add only |
+| `result_work_item_id` | UUID NULL; successful Add only, exactly one |
+| `error_code` | TEXT NULL; closed private codes only |
+| timestamps | started/completed timestamps |
+
+Unique `(tenant_id,candidate_id,idempotency_key)` on each ledger gives replay identity. Same key
+plus different hash is `409 idempotency_conflict`. A succeeded row returns the
+same result. A failed retry may re-drive only codes classified retryable. The
+candidate terminal compare-and-set decides Add-vs-Dismiss races; one wins and the
+other receives the stable terminal card.
