+
+Public decoders: `decodeMeetingReviewCardV1`, `decodeMeetingReviewListV1`,
+`decodeAddMeetingActionCandidateV1`, `decodeAdjustMeetingReviewSubjectV1`,
+`decodeDismissMeetingReviewSubjectV1`, `decodeMeetingSummaryCommandResultV1`, and
+`decodeMeetingActionCommandResultV1`. The discriminated union rejects an `add`
+action/result/destination on summary artifacts. Internal platform API Zod schemas mirror
+and drift-test those contracts; the web decodes before state mutation.
+
+### Materialization and legacy compatibility
+
+`refreshMeetingReview` is the replacement for automatic proposal ingest.
+It runs only after the caller is authorized for each meeting and:
+
+1. mints one attributable service run per meeting conversation;
+2. projects the latest final `summaries` row to the meeting's summary artifact
+   and each generated/promoted `action_items` row to an action candidate;
+3. creates one subject plus v1 only when the source key/hash is new;
+4. appends a source version only while the summary is current or action candidate
+   is pending and source content changed; dismissed/terminal subjects remain so;
+5. resolves at most three action suggestions and summary evidence links through
+   current internal IDs and omits all
+   uncertain/ambiguous values;
+6. creates zero proposals, memories, work items, checks, dependencies, or parent
+   links.
+
+The old `POST /api/agent/meeting-ingest` mutating contract is retired fail-closed.
+After the new web client switches, it returns `410` with
+`{error:'explicit_review_required'}`. It must not silently alias old “create
+proposals” semantics to refresh.
+
+Backfill is dry-run by default, deterministic, sorted, rerunnable, and uses no
+model:
+
+- create summary artifacts/v1 for recoverable final summaries and action
+  candidates/v1 for promoted action items only when PR A origin is complete;
+- map existing `meeting_promotions` and linked proposals/work items to action candidate
+  provenance;
+- `applied` legacy proposal -> `added` with the existing work item;
+- rejected/superseded/expired legacy proposal -> `dismissed` with no new work;
+- pending legacy proposal -> pending action candidate; Add reuses it and supplies the
+  displayed version as `edited_payload`; Dismiss rejects it explicitly;
+- source/mapping/origin/status ambiguity -> quarantine, no review projection;
+- unresolved suggestions are omitted, never inferred from text.
+
+The operator report contains schema/migration versions, mode, timestamps, sorted
+counts, and `{tenantId,meetingId,sourceKind,sourceKey,reasonCode}` only. It excludes
+titles, summaries, action text, rationale, labels, emails, participants, prompts,
+transcripts, evidence content, and credentials.
+
+### Shared caller authorization and projections
+
+Repository inputs receive only the verified server caller `(provider,subject)`
+plus server-selected tenant/resource. Request/model payloads cannot select user,
+actor, tenant, access conversation, visibility, role, or provenance.
+
+- List/search/injection: one bounded SQL authorization join filters before count,
+  sort, rank, embedding, projection, or model input; denied rows yield an empty
+  lane.
+- Direct read/action: load the minimal private origin, call PR A's one-statement
+  current authorization with required role, then project; missing/denied both 404.
+- Reader: list/detail/history. Writer/admin: summary Adjust/Dismiss, action
+  Add/Adjust/Dismiss, and derivative mutations. Existing org/private lanes keep
+  their rules.
+- Meeting Python routes implement the same contract/version and denial precedence
+  against the shared Neon tables; no provider/label fallback. Cross-language
+  fixtures prove the TS and Python decisions match.
+- Every proposal list/detail/accept/reject/undo/curator/active-rules path and every
+  memory list/detail/chain/supersede/retract/defer/restore/retrieval path filters
+  conversation rows by current membership.
+- Work-item list/update/activity, checks, dependencies, project aggregates,
+  agent list/get/propose, KB ingest/retrieval, reflection, and capture inherit the
+  restricted work item's access predicate. Child rows cannot reveal a denied
+  parent ID or count.
+- Action Add preserves `access_conversation_id`. No payload field or proposal edit
+  can clear it. Organization publication is not implemented here.
+
+### Action Add command and exactly-once work item
+
+Add exists only for action candidates and operates on the current version only:
+
+1. Strictly decode body; load minimal candidate origin; derive caller actor; require
+   current writer/admin membership.
+2. Insert/replay the command row and compare request hash. Re-authorize and
+   compare `expected_version_id` immediately before the winning write.
+3. Re-resolve each confirmed suggestion: current actor/user, valid date, visible
+   same-tenant parent/dependency, compatible target team/status. Missing/stale
+   values are omitted only if not confirmed; a confirmed value that became invalid
+   returns `409 stale_suggestion` and creates nothing.
+4. Create/reuse one conversation-scoped proposal uniquely keyed by candidate.
+   Proposal payload contains only the reviewed version and confirmed IDs.
+5. Apply through the existing proposal/domain command. The transaction/batch
+   writes one work item plus activity/dependencies, proposal decision,
+   candidate resolution, and command result. Any failed invariant leaves no
+   externally visible result.
+6. Replays return the same proposal/result IDs. A crash after the domain record but
+   before command closure is repaired by the existing proposal-source unique key
+   and candidate compare-and-set; it never creates a second record.
+
+`simple_task` is a deliberately minimal action:
+title plus only confirmed chips. `planned_work_item` may include confirmed parent
+and dependencies. Required Product-Suite fields use the existing validated
+domain defaults only when they are product configuration (for example a single
+configured destination team/status), never as extracted facts. Ambiguous team or
+missing status returns a fixable card error and no work item.
+
+### Subject-specific Adjust collaboration/run protocol
+
+Summary Adjust and action Adjust do not call generic `runAgentChat` because that
+prompt exposes proposal tools. They reuse the same authority and persistence
+primitives in a dedicated, tool-free runner:
+
+1. authorize writer/admin and append `message.created` for the caller with the
+   subject-specific artifact/candidate and displayed-version references; the
+   event key derives from command identity;
+2. mint one `agent_runs(kind='chat',conversation_id=<meeting conversation>,
+   thread_id=NULL)` row, triggered by the internal user;
+3. pass only the subject kind, current reviewed version, confirmed evidence IDs, and
+   the user's adjustment message as delimited untrusted data. No raw transcript,
+   denied source, retrieval tool, mutation tool, or generic workboard prompt;
+4. use AI SDK v6 structured output with the strict subject-specific codec; summary
+   output cannot contain destination or assignments, while action output may use
+   only the two destination values and <=3 suggestions;
+5. resolve/filter links/suggestions server-side, then in one transaction append
+   the assistant event, insert the matching immutable version `N+1`, and compare-
+   and-set `current_version_id` from N to N+1;
+6. re-authorize immediately before commit. Revocation, Dismiss, action Add, or
+   another winning Adjust makes the response stale and prevents a new current version;
+7. close the run `completed` or `failed` and return the stable command result.
+
+The original version and events remain immutable. Model/schema failure returns
+the candidate to a usable pending UI; the draft message remains in the browser.
+No partial version becomes current.
+
+### Distinct summary and action state machines
+
+The durable summary-artifact state machine is:
+
+```text
+current --Adjust succeeds--> current with immutable version N+1
+current --Dismiss succeeds-> dismissed-for-review (terminal queue state)
+```
+
+Dismiss never deletes or mutates the meeting's summary evidence. There is no
+summary Add transition. The durable action-candidate state machine is:
+
+```text
+pending --Adjust task/planned--> pending with immutable version N+1
+pending --Adjust keep-follow-up-> kept_as_follow_up (terminal, meeting evidence only)
+pending --Add succeeds----------> added (terminal, exactly one work item)
+pending --Dismiss succeeds------> dismissed (terminal)
+```
+
+Duplicate semantic commands return their recorded result. Stale versions return
+`409 stale_version` plus the latest safe card. Add/Dismiss races are resolved by
+one compare-and-set; the loser sees the winner's terminal state. A late Adjust
+cannot update a terminal subject. Refresh/backfill never reopen terminal rows.
+
+### API routes and response projections
+
+All routes are authenticated. The mixed feed is `/api/agent/meeting-review`;
+subject commands are separated so summary Add is unrepresentable:
+
+| Route | Contract |
+|---|---|
+| `GET /api/agent/meeting-review?org_id=&cursor=&limit=` | Bounded discriminated cards; unauthorized meetings omitted; `limit` 1..50 |
+| `POST /api/agent/meeting-review/refresh` | Materialize authorized artifacts/candidates only; counts writes, always zero Product-Suite writes |
+| `POST /api/agent/meeting-summary-artifacts/:id/adjust` | Tool-free summary revision; `201` first, `200` replay |
+| `POST /api/agent/meeting-summary-artifacts/:id/dismiss` | Remove summary from review queue; `200` first/replay |
+| `POST /api/agent/meeting-action-candidates/:id/add` | Exactly-once work item; `201` first, `200` replay |
+| `POST /api/agent/meeting-action-candidates/:id/adjust` | Tool-free action revision; `201` first, `200` replay |
+| `POST /api/agent/meeting-action-candidates/:id/dismiss` | Terminal no-work decision; `200` first/replay |
+| `GET /api/agent/meeting-review/:type/:id/adjustments?after_sequence=&limit=` | Subject-referenced conversation events only, current membership required |
+
+List envelope is exactly `{schema_version:1,items,next_cursor}` where `items` is
+the strict discriminated union. Summary command success is exactly
+`{schema_version:1,status,summary_artifact,duplicate,run_id?}`. Action command
+success is exactly
+`{schema_version:1,status,action_candidate,duplicate,proposal_id?,work_item?,run_id?}`.
+Public errors are closed: `invalid_request` 400, `not_found` 404,
+`stale_version|stale_suggestion|terminal|idempotency_conflict` 409, bounded
+`adjustment_failed` 422/502 by retryability, and generic 500. Private denial and
+database codes never serialize.
+
+No endpoint returns raw version body, confidence, evidence refs, access
+conversation, actor IDs, source run/events, request hash, prompt, or denied counts.
+The meeting/result hrefs are server-built from already-authorized IDs.
+
+## Platform-web experience
+
+Keep the stable `/w/$workspace/meetings/triage` route and replace its content, not
+the navigation contract.
+
+### Card
+
+- Native semantic list/article structure. Summary uses the installed Lucide
+  `FileText`; action item uses `ListTodo`; icons are `aria-hidden` and never emoji.
+- Header: visible type label and icon, concise title (two visual lines maximum,
+  full accessible text remains in DOM), and terminal status only when terminal.
+- Second line: one source/reason sentence. No raw extractor confidence percentage.
+- Suggestion row: 0..3 verified chips in deterministic owner -> date -> parent ->
+  dependency order. Parent/dependency chips are real links with accessible names.
+- Summary actions: native `Adjust` and `Dismiss`; there is no disabled or hidden
+  Add control. Pending action-candidate actions: native `Add`, `Adjust`, and
+  `Dismiss`. No icon-only action and no default structured field form.
+- Provenance/details use a native `<details>` after the actions and show safe
+  source/result links only; internal IDs/evidence remain hidden.
+
+### Inline Adjust
+
+- Adjust expands an inline region beneath the same card; no modal or separate chat
+  authority. Focus moves to a visibly labelled textarea and returns to Adjust when
+  collapsed.
+- Action Adjust shows at most the three approved choice buttons. They populate/send
+  natural language and do not map client-side to canonical fields. Summary Adjust
+  shows no planning choices. Free text remains valid for either subject.
+- Enter inserts a newline; `Ctrl+Enter`/`Cmd+Enter` submits; Escape collapses only
+  an empty draft. A non-empty draft is preserved.
+- During the run, disable actions for that card only, expose a polite status, and
+  retain the visible current version. On success announce “Candidate updated to
+  version N” and focus the new title. On failure retain draft and focus/announce the
+  inline error.
+
+### Loading, errors, responsiveness, and accessibility
+
+- Initial loading uses labelled skeleton cards; refresh does not replace readable
+  cards with a blank screen. Empty state explains that summaries/action items will
+  appear after a meeting; it never invites automatic task creation.
+- Per-card allowed-action pending states prevent double activation. A stale
+  conflict replaces only that card with the latest server projection. Global and
+  per-card retry errors are distinct and content-safe.
+- Added action cards remain visible with one work-item link; dismissed/kept-
+  follow-up cards remain compact and
+  non-actionable. Unknown future states decode to an inert honest card, never
+  `pending`.
+- DOM order equals visual/tab order. Buttons/links meet at least 24x24 CSS px
+  (target 44px), focus indicator is >=3:1, normal text >=4.5:1, and meaning is not
+  color-only. No positive `tabindex` or ARIA button emulation.
+- One column at 320px/400% zoom; metadata/actions wrap without horizontal scroll.
+  At wider viewports actions may align right but remain after content in DOM.
+- Persistent `aria-live='polite'` handles success/progress; `role='alert'` handles
+  actionable failure. Automated axe plus manual keyboard and NVDA verification are
+  required; automated checks alone are not completion evidence.
+
+## Privacy, security, and observability
+
+- Allowed logs/metrics: policy/schema version, operation, allowed/denied,
+  deterministic private reason, subject kind/state/version number, duplicate,
+  latency, retry class, and opaque tenant/conversation/candidate/run/command IDs.
+- Never log or metric-label auth claims/provider subject, email, participant or
+  speaker labels, meeting title, summary/action text, source reason, suggestion
+  label/value, evidence refs, prompt, user adjustment, model output, transcript,
+  proposal rationale, work-item content, token, or credentials.
+- Adjustment text and assistant response persist only as authorized conversation
+  events because history is a product requirement; they inherit meeting retention.
+  `agent_runs.summary` stores a content-free result phrase and IDs only.
+- Source/model text is untrusted data, not instruction. The adjust runner has no
+  tools, bounded input/output, strict schema, and server-side ID resolution.
+- A01 is primary: current membership on every path, uniform denial, same-tenant
+  constraints, and negative known-ID tests. A03 uses bound SQL and strict codecs.
+  A04 uses one authority graph, immutable versions, explicit Add, and no normal
+  declassification. A05 requires both DB and app guards. A07 uses verified internal
+  caller mapping. A08 uses content hashes, idempotency conflicts, immutable events,
+  and exact response contracts. A09 redacts content and distinguishes private codes.
+  A02/A06/A10 add no secrets, dependency, fetch URL, or provider trust surface.
+
+## Migration, rollout, compatibility, and rollback
+
+1. Merge PR A and capture its exact topology/migration SHA.
+2. Land contract/codecs and additive schema dormant. Run parity/fresh-clone and
+   response-key snapshots before enabling writers.
+3. Dry-run backfill, review redacted quarantine report, apply, rerun for zero
+   mutations, and run mandatory ephemeral-Neon conformance.
+4. Enable dual projection for authorized internal users: old reads shadow-compared
+   but never returned when new authorization denies. Any mismatch stops rollout.
+5. Deploy backend enforcement before the new UI. Keep legacy ingest disabled.
+6. Enable candidate refresh/commands for internal tenants, then the web flag after
+   exact-head API/DB evidence. Remove the flag only in a later cleanup.
+
+Rollback reverts application/UI layers in reverse order and leaves additive schema,
+immutable versions, commands, provenance, and access origins intact. It never drops
+data, clears origin, restores tenant-only reads, revives legacy `team/public` grants,
+re-enables automatic proposal ingest, or exposes quarantine. A forward fix repairs
+bad data. The kill switch for legacy ingest is independent of the card flag and
+defaults disabled.
+
+Compatibility rules:
+
+- existing non-meeting org/private content has NULL access origin and unchanged
+  public JSON;
+- restricted meeting derivatives are never projected by old wildcard serializers;
+- old pending meeting proposals remain reviewable through Add/Dismiss migration,
+  but no background process applies them;
+- SDK/public meeting routes retain response keys while authorization becomes
+  stricter; denied known IDs use the established not-found shape;
+- unknown future card states/actions decode inertly, not as pending.
+
+## TDD and evidence matrix
+
+### Unit/contract
+
+- JS/JSON/TypeScript contract drift; strict decoder rejection; exact public keys;
+  max-three suggestions/choices; optional uncertainty omitted, not null.
+- State transitions, canonical request hashing, replay/conflict, version chain,
+  immutable update/delete rejection, source hash dedupe, terminal refresh.
+- Suggestion resolution: exact active actor/date/item passes; ambiguous/inactive/
+  cross-tenant/unauthorized/stale/missing fails or is omitted before version write.
+- Summary codec/route/state rejects Add structurally; action Add maps only simple/
+  planned destinations. Keep-follow-up terminates promotion and writes no memory
+  or work item. Refresh, Adjust, and Dismiss create zero Product-Suite records.
+
+### Authorization/routes
+
+Use Alice (current admin), Bob (same tenant non-member), Carol (other tenant),
+Dave (removed member), and Eve (provider/label spoof):
+
+- source/summary-artifact/action-candidate/version/adjustment events, legacy
+  meeting-derived memory/chunk, proposal, work item,
+  checks/dependencies/activity/project aggregate, agent retrieval/tool/capture;
+- list omission and direct 404 for Bob/Carol/Dave/Eve; Alice positive;
+- membership removed between two calls and immediately before Adjust/Add commit;
+- missing/mismatched origin, archived conversation, disabled actor, malformed ID,
+  and database failure deny without content/count/timing-specific response.
+
+### Concurrency and real Neon
+
+- two refreshes create one summary artifact/v1 and one action candidate/v1 with
+  zero Product-Suite records;
+- same Add key twice and two concurrent Add keys create one proposal/result;
+- summary Adjust vs Dismiss and action Add vs Dismiss/keep-follow-up have one
+  terminal/current winner;
+- crash/retry at command claim, proposal create, domain write, dependencies, proposal
+  flip, candidate resolve, and response returns one stable result;
+- same idempotency key/different request conflicts; stale version/suggestion creates
+  nothing; confirmed parent/dependencies preserve DAG/team/current access;
+- FK/check/immutability triggers reject cross-tenant and partial provenance;
+- backfill dry/apply/reapply deterministic; legacy states map without new work;
+- response-key snapshots unchanged; migration fresh-clone/parity and cleanup
+  execute nonzero tests. Missing credentials/skip/zero tests/timeout is INCOMPLETE.
+
+### Platform-web/Playwright
+
+- mixed summary-artifact/action-candidate order, correct type labels/icons,
+  concise copy, 0..3 chips,
+  safe links, pending/added/dismissed cards, inert unknown state;
+- summary has no Add control/request; action Add sends displayed version and visible
+  suggestion IDs once; retry/double-click renders one work-item link; no task before Add;
+- action Adjust shows <=3 exact choices while summary shows none; both support free
+  text, immutable revised version, stale/fail
+  recovery, draft retention, focus return, and success announcement;
+- Dismiss is stable after reload and creates no work;
+- keyboard-only, axe, NVDA announcement script, 320px, 400% zoom, reduced motion,
+  slow request, offline/error, and per-card/global loading behavior.
+
